The collection of level curves is graphed in Figure 2.16. 
The sections by x = c are 

	{(x, y, z) | z = y² - x², x = c} = {(c, y, z) | z = y² - c²}. 

These are clearly parabolas in the planes x = c. 
The sections by y = c are 

	{(x, y, z) | z = y² - x², y = c} = {(c, y, z) | z = c² - x²}, 

which are again parabolas. 
The level curves and sections generate the contour curves and surface depicted in figure 2.17. 
